  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In addition, the Lead agency in its capacity as co-lead of the Gender &amp; Protection Cluster, supports the integration of protection approaches into both its own work and the wider response.  Currently, the Lead agency is supporting the data management of the Cluster&apos;s Gender &amp; Protection Needs Assessment, providing daily needs data for decision-making through an interactive dashboard.  Once the collection exercise is concluded, this support will involve a detailed analysis of the data collected and the formulation of protection actions and recommendations to be shared response-wide as a Gender &amp; Protection Analysis Report.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Additional work through the Gender &amp; Protection Cluster includes refreshing guidance to responders on safeguarding (including child protection, PSHEA, and GBV referral pathways). The Lead agency will also be providing refresher training to staff and volunteers on all of these areas and reporting mechanisms as per organisational Code of Conduct policies.</narrative>
  </description>
